# Cutter, Genealogical and Personal Memoirs (1910), Tufts entries. Public domain; short quotes only.
CUT_ID = {1: "genealogicalpers01cutt", 2: "genealogicalpers02cutt", 3: "genealogicalpers03cutt", 4: "genealogicalpers04cutt"}
CUTTER = "William Richard Cutter, ed., <em>Genealogical and Personal Memoirs Relating to the Families of the State of Massachusetts</em> (New York: Lewis Historical Publishing Co., 1910)"
def CUT(vol, pg): return f'Cutter, <em>Genealogical and Personal Memoirs</em>, vol. {"I II III IV".split()[vol-1]}, p. {pg}. <a href="https://archive.org/details/{CUT_ID[vol]}/page/{pg}/mode/1up">Page (Internet Archive)</a>'
CUT_NOTE = '<p class="note">Cutter&rsquo;s Tufts sketch (vol. II, pp. 1198&ndash;1200) is a compiled family history of 1910, written for a descendant&rsquo;s line. Quotes are from the Internet Archive&rsquo;s scanned text, checked against the printed page numbers.</p>'
CUT_P = {
"peter-tufts-1617": Q("Peter Tufts, the immigrant ancestor, was born in England, in 1616, probably in the southern part of county Norfolk", CUT(2, 1198))
 + Q("was the ferryman with his brother-in-law. He resided on the Malden side of the river, where the city of Everett is now located", CUT(2, 1198))
 + '<p>Cutter adds that he was admitted a freeman May 3, 1665, and that his will, dated March 1, 1693, with a codicil of July 8, 1695, was proved June 10, 1700. It names his wife Mary, sons Peter, Jonathan and John, daughters Mary Eades, Elizabeth Lynde, Mercy Waite and Sarah Oakes, and his grandson James. Cutter gives his death as May 13, 1700, &ldquo;aged eighty-three,&rdquo; and his wife as &ldquo;Mary Pierce, who died January 10, 1702-3, aged seventy-five, daughter of Thomas and Elizabeth Pierce&rdquo; (vol. II, p. 1198). This is the first printed source on this page to name Mary&rsquo;s parents; it is a compiled work and gives no record behind them.</p>'
 + Q("James, son of Peter Tufts, was born in Charlestown, about 1650. He was a soldier in King Philip&rsquo;s war, and was killed in the battle of Bloody Brook, September 18, 1675.", CUT(2, 1198), note="(OCR text corrected only for obvious scanning errors.)")
 + UNV("Birth year: Cutter prints 1616; the stone&rsquo;s &ldquo;aged 83&rdquo; at his death in May 1700 gives about 1617. Cutter&rsquo;s year for the start of his ferry service is unclear in the scanned text; Corey (p. 85, n. 53) has him succeeding Drinker a few months before June 1647."),
"william-tufts-13-6": Q("William, son of James (2) Tufts, was born June 10, 1713, and died at Medford, October 29, 1783, aged seventy, according to his gravestone.", CUT(2, 1199))
 + '<p>Cutter places him in the line of the immigrant&rsquo;s son James, killed at Bloody Brook in 1675, and grandson James (1672&ndash;1733), who lived at Salem before moving to Charlestown in 1704 and died at Medford. William was the seventh child of James and his first wife, Ruth (vol. II, pp. 1198&ndash;1199).</p>'
 + Q("He married (first) February 28, 1732-3, Catherine Wyman, of an old Woburn family. She died February 20, 1748-9, aged thirty-two", CUT(2, 1199))
 + Q("He married (second) February 8, 1750, Mary Francis, who died December 1, 1812, aged ninety-three.", CUT(2, 1199))
 + '<p>Cutter lists thirteen children born at Medford: by Catherine, Catherine (who married William Tufts Jr., son of John), <a href="{P}profiles/william-tufts-40-2.html">William</a>, <a href="{P}profiles/george-tufts-40-7.html">George</a>, <a href="{P}profiles/grimes-tufts-40-8.html">Grimes</a> and Uriah; by Mary, Mary, <a href="{P}profiles/samuel-tufts-41-2.html">Samuel</a> (born August 19, 1752), Lucy (who married Thomas Pritchard), Francis, <a href="{P}profiles/david-tufts-41-7.html">David</a>, Richard (born November 17, 1763), <a href="{P}profiles/moses-tufts-40-6.html">Moses</a> and Aaron (vol. II, p. 1199).</p>'
 + UNV("Cutter puts Moses, Aaron and David among the children of the second wife, Mary Francis, married 1750. That does not fit Moses&rsquo;s 1744 baptism on his own page, and Cutter&rsquo;s date for David (June 20, 1758) differs from the 1763 on David&rsquo;s page. Brooks (p. 550) lists Moses without a mother. Cutter&rsquo;s list is not followed where it conflicts."),
"william-tufts-40-2": Q("William (2), son of William (1) Tufts, was born March 27, 1736, and died according to the church record of dropsy and jaundice, April 27, 1782.", CUT(2, 1199))
 + Q("There were several of this name in the revolution, and the writer is unable to determine whether any of the service described belongs to this William Tufts.", CUT(2, 1199))
 + '<p>Cutter gives his wife as Susannah (surname not given), who &ldquo;died at Boston, February 26, 1801, aged sixty-six, and buried in Medford.&rdquo; Their children, born at Medford, were <a href="{P}profiles/nathan-tufts-jr.html">Nathan</a> (baptized May 18, 1760), Susanna, Elinor, Aaron (December 18, 1761), William (baptized May 18, 1760) and Uriah (vol. II, p. 1199).</p>'
 + '<p>Uriah (1768&ndash;1837) became a Boston blacksmith with a smithy on Constitution Wharf. Cutter writes that &ldquo;He forged and drove the first bolts that were used in the construction of the famous frigate &lsquo;Constitution&rsquo;&rdquo; (vol. II, p. 1199).</p>'
 + UNV("Cutter&rsquo;s doubt about this William&rsquo;s war service applies to the service record on this page, which comes from a different source. Which William Tufts served in the guards company is not settled."),
"nathan-tufts-jr": Q("Nathan, born May 16, 1734, baptized May 18, 1760.", CUT(2, 1199), note="(As read in the scanned text.)")
 + '<p>Cutter thus names Nathan as the eldest child of <a href="{P}profiles/william-tufts-40-2.html">William Tufts Jr.</a> and his wife Susannah, matching Brooks&rsquo;s placement above.</p>'
 + UNV("Birth year: the scanned text prints 1734, which is before his father&rsquo;s birth in 1736 and must be a misprint or scanning error. 1754 is the likely reading; the printed page has not yet been checked against the scan."),
"grimes-tufts-40-8": Q("Grimes, born December 4, 1748.", CUT(2, 1199)) + '<p>Cutter lists him among the children of <a href="{P}profiles/william-tufts-13-6.html">William Tufts</a> and his first wife, Catherine Wyman. The birth date agrees with the one above.</p>',
"george-tufts-40-7": '<p>Cutter lists George among the children of <a href="{P}profiles/william-tufts-13-6.html">William Tufts</a> and his first wife, Catherine Wyman, born January 10 (vol. II, p. 1199).</p>' + UNV("The year in the scanned text is unclear (it reads &ldquo;1737&rdquo;); this page gives 1746/7. The printed page has not yet been checked against the scan."),
"samuel-tufts-41-2": Q("Samuel, born August 19, 1752.", CUT(2, 1199)) + '<p>Cutter lists him as a son of <a href="{P}profiles/william-tufts-13-6.html">William Tufts</a> by his second wife, Mary Francis. The birth date agrees with the one above.</p>',
"david-tufts-41-7": Q("David, born June 20, 1758.", CUT(2, 1199)) + '<p>Cutter lists him as a son of <a href="{P}profiles/william-tufts-13-6.html">William Tufts</a> by his second wife, Mary Francis.</p>' + UNV("Birth date: Cutter gives June 20, 1758; this page gives June 17, 1763. A 1758 birth would make him about sixteen, not eleven, at Concord in 1775. Note: Pending further work."),
"moses-tufts-40-6": '<p>Cutter lists a Moses among the children of <a href="{P}profiles/william-tufts-13-6.html">William Tufts</a>, placed with the children of his second wife, Mary Francis (vol. II, p. 1199). He gives no dates for him.</p>' + UNV("Cutter&rsquo;s placement under the second wife (married 1750) conflicts with a 1744 baptism. Whether Cutter&rsquo;s Moses is this man is not settled."),
"aaron-tufts": '<p>Cutter names two Aarons in this family: a son of <a href="{P}profiles/william-tufts-13-6.html">Lieut. William Tufts</a> (no dates), and a grandson, born December 18, 1761, son of <a href="{P}profiles/william-tufts-40-2.html">William Tufts Jr.</a> and Susannah (vol. II, p. 1199).</p>' + UNV("Which Aaron, if either, is the Continental soldier on this page is not established."),
"francis-tufts-41-4": '<p>Cutter lists a Francis among the children of <a href="{P}profiles/william-tufts-13-6.html">William Tufts</a> and Mary Francis, with no dates, noting only that he &ldquo;married ____ Francis&rdquo; (vol. II, p. 1199).</p>' + UNV("Cutter gives no birth date or place, so it is not known whether his Francis is the Lancaster-born Francis Tufts (1756&ndash;1823) on this page."),
"simon-tufts-11-1": Q("Dr. Tufts took him into his family at the age of fourteen to educate for his profession. He continued with Dr. Tufts until he was twenty-one years old. The doctor then advised him to begin the practice of medicine in the adjoining town of Reading", CUT(1, 566))
 + '<p>Cutter&rsquo;s sketch of Governor John Brooks repeats this account of his apprenticeship to Dr. Tufts of Medford.</p>',
}
_EXTRA_CUT = EXTRA
def EXTRA(path):
    out = _EXTRA_CUT(path)
    s = path[9:-5] if path.startswith("profiles/") else ""
    if s in CUT_P:
        out += '{DIV}<section id="cutter"><h2>From Cutter&rsquo;s Memoirs (1910)</h2>' + CUT_P[s] + CUT_NOTE + '<p class="cite">Source added: ' + CUTTER + '.</p></section>'
    return out
